# Line endings, settled once so they cannot drift per machine.
#
# `.editorconfig` already declares `end_of_line = lf`, but an editorconfig is
# a hint to editors — it has no say in what git writes to the working tree.
# With no `.gitattributes`, that was decided entirely by each developer's local
# `core.autocrlf`, and on a Windows checkout (`autocrlf=true`, the installer
# default) the result was a working tree with 250 CRLF files against 351 LF
# ones. The repository blobs were fine throughout; the inconsistency was local,
# and it is the kind that produces whole-file diffs the moment two machines
# with different settings touch the same file.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises every text file to LF in the repository AND on
# checkout, on every platform, regardless of anyone's local git config. That
# matches `.editorconfig`, and it matches what the blobs already contain, so
# adding this changes no committed content.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched. Listing them explicitly is cheaper than
# trusting content detection on a file that happens to start with ASCII.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.pdf binary
